// "Single instantaneous pulse along the line (not a sustained beam)" per
// the sheet's own notes. `BasicBeam` (common/src/states/basic_beam.rs) has
// no separate "instant line" mode -- it always spawns a `beam::Beam`
// entity that ticks for `beam_duration` seconds at `tick_rate` ticks/sec.
// Approximated as a near-zero-duration channel: `beam_duration: 0.25` with
// `tick_rate: 5.0` (tick_dur = 0.2s) guarantees exactly one damage tick
// fires before the beam ends, reading as a single pulse rather than a
// sustained drain -- contrast witch_bolt.ron in this same folder, whose
// `beam_duration: 60` is a genuine sustained channel.
//
// `damage_kind` is not RON-configurable on `BasicBeam` -- it hardcodes
// `DamageKind::Energy` unconditionally (common/src/states/basic_beam.rs:
// `Damage { kind: DamageKind::Energy, .. }`) -- so despite the "silver
// force" flavor text this deals generic Energy damage under the hood, not
// `Force` (same category of drift as Explosion/GroundAoe's own hardcoded
// DamageKind elsewhere in this batch). `specifier: Lightning` is a
// cosmetic-only choice (no `Force`/generic-arcane beam specifier exists in
// `beam::FrontendSpecifier`) for the brightest available beam VFX; it has
// no mechanical effect.
//
// Circle 3: `energy_drain: 140` over the 0.25s pulse spends ~35 energy
// total, in the same band as this wave's other circle-3 spells
// (cacophonic_shield/mass_healing_word: 55, fireball: 90). Flagged for
// wave-close-out balance review as the first player-spell single-pulse
// `BasicBeam`.
BasicBeam(
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.35,
    beam_duration: 0.25,
    damage: 34.0,
    tick_rate: 5.0,
    range: 37.0,
    max_angle: 5.0,
    damage_effect: None,
    energy_regen: 0,
    energy_drain: 140,
    move_efficiency: 0.3,
    ori_rate: 0.3,
    specifier: Lightning,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
